## Canonical AI Engineering Guides 

- [LLM Evaluation](https://arize.com/resources/llm-evaluation/): Definitive guide to evaluating LLM applications with datasets, experiments, code-based evaluators, LLM-as-a-Judge, production evaluation, and feedback loops.
- [AI Agent Tracing and Evaluation](https://arize.com/resources/ai-agent-tracing-evaluation/): Developer guide to tracing and evaluating agents across spans, traces, trajectories, tool calls, sessions, and task outcomes.
- [AI Agent Handbook](https://arize.com/guides/ai-agent-handbook/): Guide to building, evaluating, observing, and operating AI agents.
- [Agent Evaluation](https://arize.com/guides/ai-agent-handbook/agent-evaluation/): This guide explains how to build agent evaluations, representative datasets, trace complete runs, decide between the right evaluators, compare changes, and turn production failures into regression tests. 
- [Agent Evaluation Metrics](https://arize.com/guides/ai-agent-handbook/agent-evaluation-metrics/): Framework for measuring agent task success, path quality, tool use, reliability, latency, cost, safety, and business outcomes.
- [Agent Observability and Tracing](https://arize.com/guides/ai-agent-handbook/agent-observability/): Guide to monitoring and debugging agent behavior through traces, spans, tool calls, sessions, and production signals.
- [LLM-as-a-Judge](https://arize.com/guides/llm-as-a-judge/): Guide to building, calibrating, validating, and operating model-based evaluators.
- [Agent Harness](https://arize.com/resources/agent-harness-evaluation-tracing/): Guide to the runtime and control layer around an AI agent, including tools, context, state, permissions, persistence, tracing, evaluation, and the agent improvement loop.
- [Evaluation Harness](https://arize.com/blog/what-is-an-evaluation-harness/): Guide to the infrastructure used to run datasets, evaluators, experiments, regression tests, and release gates.
- [AI Agent Frameworks](https://arize.com/guides/ai-agent-handbook/agent-frameworks/): Comparison of agent frameworks including LangGraph, CrewAI, AutoGen, and other approaches, with guidance on architecture, orchestration, state, tools, and framework selection.
- [LLM Evaluation Metrics](https://arize.com/resources/llm-evaluation/metrics/): Guide to choosing evaluation metrics for correctness, groundedness, retrieval, agent behavior, task success, and other LLM application quality dimensions.
- [Pre-Production LLM Evaluation](https://arize.com/resources/llm-evaluation/pre-production-llm-evaluation/): Guide to building evaluation datasets, generating synthetic data, establishing benchmarks, and testing LLM applications before release.
- [CI/CD for LLM Applications](https://arize.com/resources/llm-evaluation/ci-cd-for-llm-apps/): Guide to experiments, regression testing, evaluation-driven development, and release gates for LLM applications.
- [Production LLM Evaluation](https://arize.com/resources/llm-evaluation/production-llm-evaluation/): Guide to online evaluations, guardrails, sampling, monitoring, and detecting quality failures in production.
- [Self-Improving LLM Evaluation](https://arize.com/resources/llm-evaluation/self-improving-llm-evaluation/): Guide to closing the evaluation feedback loop by turning production failures into datasets, evaluator improvements, experiments, and application changes.
- [What Is AI Engineering?](https://arize.com/resources/what-is-ai-engineering/): Field guide to AI engineering as the discipline of building, observing, evaluating, and continuously improving applications built on LLMs and agents.
- [What Is an Agent Observability Platform?](https://arize.com/resources/whats-an-agent-observability-platform/): Guide to agent observability architecture and how tracing, evaluation, production monitoring, datasets, and experiments work together.
- [AI Agent Testing](https://arize.com/resources/ai-agent-testing/): Guide to testing agent behavior beyond traditional software tests, including task, tool, trajectory, recovery, and session-level failures.
- [Harness Engineering](https://arize.com/resources/harness-engineering/): Guide to governing agent runtimes with task contracts, capability boundaries, permissions, completion gates, durable state, verification, and recovery.
- [The Agent Reliability Gap](https://arize.com/resources/agent-reliability-gap/): Research-backed framework for closing the gap between plausible agent outputs and dependable production execution — failure taxonomy, trace schema, runtime governance, and a 30-day implementation plan.

## Choosing AI Engineering Infrastructure

- [LLM and Agent Evaluation Platforms](https://arize.com/resources/llm-and-agent-evaluation-platforms/): Comparison of evaluation platforms across tracing, datasets, experiments, offline and online evaluation, human review, agent evaluation, deployment, and production workflows.
- [AI Agent Debugging Tools](https://arize.com/resources/best-ai-agent-debugging-tools/): Comparison of production agent debugging platforms across failure discovery, diagnosis, reproduction, regression testing, remediation, and recurrence detection.
- [Self-Hosted AI Observability](https://arize.com/resources/self-hosted-ai-observability/): Guide to SaaS, BYOC, hybrid, open-source, private, and air-gapped AI observability deployments, including a checklist for evaluating what actually runs inside a customer's infrastructure.
- [AI Agent Analytics Platforms](https://arize.com/resources/agent-analytics-buyers-guide/): Buyer’s guide to connecting agent behavior and technical quality signals with task completion, adoption, conversion, support cost, and other business outcomes.

